        <section class="section-surface" id="server-participant"><div class="shell section-pad benchmark-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">For server and data-center operators</p><h2>Bring one machine. Help build the public baseline.</h2><p class="section-lede">Start with one server or rack you can measure safely. The first participation path is a locally run, documented measurement—not handing the project control of production hardware.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" data-contact-link href="/CONTRIBUTING.md">Tell us about your system</a><a class="button secondary" href="/challenge/#baseline">See the measurement steps</a><a class="button secondary" href="/docs/QUIET_COMPUTE_CONTRIBUTION_TERMS_DRAFT.md">Read the draft terms</a></div></div><div class="benchmark-card"><div><span>You provide</span><strong>Declared hardware, workload, sound, temperature, power, and environment data</strong></div><div><span>You keep</span><strong>Credentials, remote access, control of the machine, and unrelated private data</strong></div><div><span>We publish</span><strong>Only the artifact scope and commercial-use permission you deliberately declare</strong></div><div><span>We do not claim</span><strong>That one server represents every data center or that a baseline proves a solution</strong></div></div></div></section>
